# D-105 native, the result route (steps/d105-native.md §5): `id (Model: m)
# Model` returns its formal, which `o: Other` reached: the formal's edge carries Other to id's result, id's
# return records the value (already recorded -- the same pair), and `rd(id(o))` reads 10.  Before: 20.
# Success is 7.
Model:
    size_t: a 1U
    size_t: b 2U
end: Model
Other:
    size_t: b 20U
    size_t: a 10U
end: Other
fn: rd (Model: m) size_t
return: m\a
fn: id (Model: m) Model
return: m
fn: go () size_t
    Other: o
    return: rd(id(o))
size_t: got 0U
got: go()
int: ok 3
if: got = 10U
    ok: 7
if: got = 20U
    ok: 5
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
